WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Assumptions shape how people interpret information.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Sometimes they are accurate.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Sometimes they are outdated, incomplete, or incorrect.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.520
An assumptions check involves identifying the beliefs underlying an assessment and asking

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.000
whether they remain valid.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.000
What are we assuming?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Why are we assuming it?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.000
What evidence supports those assumptions?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
The technique also asks what would happen if an assumption proved false.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
That question can reveal fragile reasoning, information gaps,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
or areas where the assessment needs caveats.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Making assumptions visible improves analytical quality.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.300
It helps teams challenge default thinking without treating every disagreement as personal.
